 3      IgnDupl: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
$INDEXER "$DIR" "$IDX"

# 1. command-line argument checks

# no arguments at all, so it should print usage
./querier
usage: ./querier pageDirectory indexFilename

# only one argument, still wrong, should print usage
./querier $DIR
usage: ./querier pageDirectory indexFilename

# three arguments, one too many, should print usage
./querier $DIR $IDX extra
usage: ./querier pageDirectory indexFilename

# page directory that doesn't exist, should say it's not a crawler dir
./querier $BAD $IDX
Error: '/no/such/path' is not a crawler directory

# page directory that exists but has no .crawler sentinel, same complaint
./querier . $IDX
Error: '.' is not a crawler directory

# index file that doesn't exist, should say it can't read the index
./querier $DIR $BAD
Error: cannot read index from '/no/such/path'

# 2. ranked queries against the real crawled-and-indexed letters site
# every page links 'home', so a 'home' query matches all 9 documents.
# the index page is the only one carrying 'playground' and 'tse'.
# and/or operators let me intersect and union the matching sets.

./querier $DIR $IDX <<EOF
home
tse
playground
breadth or depth
breadth and depth
fast and fourier and transform
computational and biology
home and tse
playground or eniac
EOF
Query: home
Matches 9 documents (ranked):
score   2 doc    1: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
score   1 doc    2: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/A.html
score   1 doc    3: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/B.html
score   1 doc    4: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/E.html
score   1 doc    5: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/G.html
score   1 doc    6: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/H.html
score   1 doc    7: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/F.html
score   1 doc    8: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/D.html
score   1 doc    9: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/C.html
Query: tse
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    1: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
Query: playground
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    1: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
Query: breadth or depth
Matches 2 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    3: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/B.html
score   1 doc    8: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/D.html
Query: breadth and depth
No documents match.
Query: fast and fourier and transform
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    7: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/F.html
Query: computational and biology
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    9: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/C.html
Query: home and tse
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    1: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
Query: playground or eniac
Matches 2 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    1: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
score   1 doc    4: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/E.html

# 3. the syntax error messages from the spec
# operator-first, operator-last, two-operators-adjacent, and the
# bad-character cases are all here

./querier $DIR $IDX <<EOF
and
or
and earth
or earth
planet earth or
planet earth and
planet earth and or science
planet earth and and science
planet earth or and science
Warning!
(The Lunar Chronicles #4.5)
git-flow
EOF
Query: and
Error: 'and' cannot be first
Query: or
Error: 'or' cannot be first
Query: and earth
Error: 'and' cannot be first
Query: or earth
Error: 'or' cannot be first
Query: planet earth or
Error: 'or' cannot be last
Query: planet earth and
Error: 'and' cannot be last
Query: planet earth and or science
Error: 'and' and 'or' cannot be adjacent
Query: planet earth and and science
Error: 'and' and 'and' cannot be adjacent
Query: planet earth or and science
Error: 'or' and 'and' cannot be adjacent
Error: bad character '!' in query.
Error: bad character '(' in query.
Error: bad character '-' in query.

# 4. whitespace, case folding, short words, and empty input
./querier $DIR $IDX <<EOF
   BREADTH    first
   home   AND   tse
a home tse
EOF
Query: breadth first
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    3: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/B.html
Query: home and tse
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    1: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/index.html
Query: a home tse
No documents match.

# empty input file, the querier should just exit cleanly with no output
./querier $DIR $IDX </dev/null

# 5. one big scripted batch of queries in a single run
./querier $DIR $IDX <<EOF
algorithm
graph
traversal
algorithm graph
algorithm or traversal
algorithm and traversal
notInTheIndex
EOF
Query: algorithm
Matches 1 documents (ranked):
score   1 doc    2: http://cs50tse.cs.dartmouth.edu/tse/letters/A.html
